{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have not eaten of it in my mourning.</b> (And I have not ruined it in impurity, and) I have not stolen from it — like 'his hands restore his wealth' (Job 20:10)." "<b>And I have not cleared away from it.</b> I have not ruined it <b>in impurity</b> — with an impure thing. For it is forbidden to remove anything from the grain before the tithe, which is sacred, has been separated from it." "<b>And I have not given of it to the dead.</b> But to You I have brought it and given it, for You are Elohim of the living and King of the universe." "<b>I have done according to all that You commanded me.</b> Regarding first fruits and regarding tithes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:22.051983161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}